{
  "case_id": "2022-22-381",
  "document_hash": "3637675ef23b2e24cbefffc084a0828ec4d83fd773ff20e5a24ec20d9c4d46db",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2022-22-381",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3637675ef23b2e24cbefffc084a0828ec4d83fd773ff20e5a24ec20d9c4d46db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3637675ef23b-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument this morning in Case 22-381, Yegiazaryan versus Smagin. Mr. Levy."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Vincent Levy",
      "case_id": "2022-22-381",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3637675ef23b2e24cbefffc084a0828ec4d83fd773ff20e5a24ec20d9c4d46db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3637675ef23b-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. LEVY: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: In RJR Nabisco, the Court held that private plaintiffs may sue under civil RICO for treble damages if they suffer a domestic injury."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-22-381",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3637675ef23b2e24cbefffc084a0828ec4d83fd773ff20e5a24ec20d9c4d46db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3637675ef23b-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Mr. Levy, you seem to, in your brief and in your opening statement, argue that all property, injury involving all property, the injury accrues at the domicile of the party. How would you deal with real property using your approach?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Vincent Levy",
      "case_id": "2022-22-381",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3637675ef23b2e24cbefffc084a0828ec4d83fd773ff20e5a24ec20d9c4d46db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3637675ef23b-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. LEVY: Well, there's no law that supports the notion that that judgment exists in California or in the United States. The common law has long looked at intangibles as following the person of the creditor. Blodgett makes the point in 1928, and the principle goes back to Justice Story's Commentaries that -- that a property right that is intangible, such as a debt, follows the creditor."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Levy",
      "case_id": "2022-22-381",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3637675ef23b2e24cbefffc084a0828ec4d83fd773ff20e5a24ec20d9c4d46db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3637675ef23b-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our position is that the court should look to the Restatement rules to determine where the injury was found and where it occurred."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2022-22-381",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3637675ef23b2e24cbefffc084a0828ec4d83fd773ff20e5a24ec20d9c4d46db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3637675ef23b-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And so the ALI was doing something more aspirational, is kind of your -- your argument? It was pushing for a change, not existing?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-22-381",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3637675ef23b2e24cbefffc084a0828ec4d83fd773ff20e5a24ec20d9c4d46db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3637675ef23b-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is it true, though, that even before the Second Restatement was adopted, that a number of states had abandoned the First Restatement and had adopted something more like the Second, including, incidentally, Heritage Reporting Corporation"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Levy",
      "case_id": "2022-22-381",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3637675ef23b2e24cbefffc084a0828ec4d83fd773ff20e5a24ec20d9c4d46db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3637675ef23b-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the Court has made clear that the presumption is a different canon of interpretation than the note -- than -- than the canon against considering prescriptive comity."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-22-381",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3637675ef23b2e24cbefffc084a0828ec4d83fd773ff20e5a24ec20d9c4d46db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3637675ef23b-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In the RJR case, didn't the Court also say that we had a context-specific kind of dynamic working here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-22-381",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3637675ef23b2e24cbefffc084a0828ec4d83fd773ff20e5a24ec20d9c4d46db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3637675ef23b-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What specifically was the intangible asset that was the basis for the Ninth Circuit's decision here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-22-381",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3637675ef23b2e24cbefffc084a0828ec4d83fd773ff20e5a24ec20d9c4d46db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3637675ef23b-0001-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So, in your argument then, the debt is the intangible property?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Nicholas O. Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2022-22-381",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3637675ef23b2e24cbefffc084a0828ec4d83fd773ff20e5a24ec20d9c4d46db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3637675ef23b-0001-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Smagin states a RICO claim because he alleged injury to his California property from California action that violates RICO. RJR Nabisco teaches us that a domestic injury is one that arises in the United States."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Nicholas O. Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2022-22-381",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3637675ef23b2e24cbefffc084a0828ec4d83fd773ff20e5a24ec20d9c4d46db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3637675ef23b-0001-0010",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Petitioners' attempt to escape RICO liability simply because their victim lives abroad should fail for two reasons. First, the text. Section 1964(c) allows any person injured in their business or property to bring a civil RICO claim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Nicholas O. Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2022-22-381",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3637675ef23b2e24cbefffc084a0828ec4d83fd773ff20e5a24ec20d9c4d46db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3637675ef23b-0001-0012",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First, Mr. Yegiazaryan moved to California and has lived in California, enjoying the benefits and the protections of U.S. law for over a decade."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Nicholas O. Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2022-22-381",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3637675ef23b2e24cbefffc084a0828ec4d83fd773ff20e5a24ec20d9c4d46db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3637675ef23b-0001-0013",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I don't believe we would, Your Honor, because RJR Nabisco teaches us that it must be conduct-focused."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Nicholas O. Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2022-22-381",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3637675ef23b2e24cbefffc084a0828ec4d83fd773ff20e5a24ec20d9c4d46db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3637675ef23b-0001-0014",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I believe RJR focuses on both, as does the text."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2022-22-381",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "3637675ef23b2e24cbefffc084a0828ec4d83fd773ff20e5a24ec20d9c4d46db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3637675ef23b-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Well, it sounds like you have a better argument from precedent than from statutory text, right? The statutory text just says property. It's our precedent that suggests that we generally look to conduct."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-22-381",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "3637675ef23b2e24cbefffc084a0828ec4d83fd773ff20e5a24ec20d9c4d46db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3637675ef23b-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Could you -- could you comment on the comity question that was posed to Mr. Levy? But, in doing that, let's change the facts and assume that both the plaintiff and the defendant here are British so that, presumably, the -- the debt could be collected in Britain. Does it -- what would be the comity implications there of allowing this to -- to take -- allowing a -- a RICO claim of this sort to go ahead in the United States?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2022-22-381",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3637675ef23b2e24cbefffc084a0828ec4d83fd773ff20e5a24ec20d9c4d46db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3637675ef23b-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "One, I would say there has been no foreign amicus briefs here, as in the other extraterritoriality cases. Two, that is because there's not -- we're not talking about foreign conduct here. We're talking about domestic conduct. And, three, that's why I don't think we get to the --the Heritage Reporting Corporation"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Smagin",
      "case_id": "2022-22-381",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3637675ef23b2e24cbefffc084a0828ec4d83fd773ff20e5a24ec20d9c4d46db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3637675ef23b-0003-0001",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Smagin states a RICO claim because he alleged injury to Heritage Reporting Corporation"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Vincent Levy",
      "case_id": "2022-22-381",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3637675ef23b2e24cbefffc084a0828ec4d83fd773ff20e5a24ec20d9c4d46db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3637675ef23b-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "My friends agree that RICO covers economic injury alone, and -- and they have to. The text of the statute so says."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-22-381",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3637675ef23b2e24cbefffc084a0828ec4d83fd773ff20e5a24ec20d9c4d46db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3637675ef23b-0003-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There's a 20-year limitation period for recognizing judgments and for enforcing them."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2022-22-381",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3637675ef23b2e24cbefffc084a0828ec4d83fd773ff20e5a24ec20d9c4d46db",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3637675ef23b-0003-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "(Whereupon, at 11:07 a.m., the case was submitted.)"
    },
    {
